n", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [77, 79]}, {"id": 79, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[95, 95]], "assertion": "since the CI includes zero and p=0.074 exceeds the threshold, the result is characterized as inconclusive rather than definitively null", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval", "p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [77, 78]}, {"id": 80, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[96, 96]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 81, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[97, 97]], "note": "magnitude and uncertainty subheading"}, {"id": 82, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[98, 98]], "assertion": "the estimated effect (0.17 pp) is substantively small, representing about a 13.5% relative increase over the 1.26% baseline rate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 83, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[99, 99]], "assertion": "the CI is wide, spanning a slight protective effect to a moderate risk increase, with the upper bound representing a 29% relative increase", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 84, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[100, 100]], "assertion": "the study was underpowered to detect an effect of this magnitude, with the MDE for 80% power (0.22 pp) exceeding the observed effect (0.17 pp)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 85, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[101, 101]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 86, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[102, 102]], "note": "direction subheading"}, {"id": 87, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[103, 103]], "assertion": "the effect is consistently in the hypothesized direction across all model specifications, lending some credibility despite non-significance", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction consistency"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 88, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[104, 106]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 89, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[107, 108]], "note": "sensitivity analyses heading"}, {"id": 90, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[109, 109]], "assertion": "multiple robustness checks were performed to test the stability of the findings", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 91, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[110, 111]], "note": "alternative skin tone categorizations subheading"}, {"id": 92, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[112, 112]], "assertion": "using a conservative categorization (≤0.25 vs ≥0.75), the adjusted risk difference was 0.224 pp (95% CI [-0.009, 0.457], p=0.059), still non-significant but closer to significance", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conservative skin tone categorization"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 93, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[113, 113]], "assertion": "treating skin tone as continuous, each 1-unit increase was associated with a 0.287 pp increase in red card probability (95% CI [0.008, 0.565], p=0.044)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [94]}, {"id": 94, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[113, 113]], "assertion": "the continuous skin tone specification was statistically significant, suggesting a dose-response relationship", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [93]}, {"id": 95, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[114, 115]], "note": "heterogeneity by league subheading"}, {"id": 96, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[116, 116]], "assertion": "substantial variation across leagues was found (LR test χ