covariates, though unmeasured confounding remains possible", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding by measured covariates"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [104]}, {"id": 106, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[126, 128]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[129, 130]], "note": "limitations and sources of bias heading"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[131, 131]], "note": "statistical power subheading"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[132, 132]], "assertion": "the study lacks sufficient power (43% post-hoc power, 57% chance of Type II error if the true effect is 0.17pp), and a larger sample or longer follow-up would be needed to definitively test the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[133, 133]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[134, 134]], "note": "rare outcome subheading"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[135, 135]], "assertion": "red cards occur in only 1.26% of dyads, creating a highly imbalanced outcome that may violate model assumptions, though logistic regression is designed for binary outcomes", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red card rarity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[136, 136]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "unmeasured confounding subheading"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[138, 138]], "assertion": "the analysis cannot rule out confounding by player behavior or referee-specific factors, since position/league/exposure adjustment may not fully capture behavioral differences correlated with skin tone", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["unmeasured confounding"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "measurement error in skin tone subheading"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "skin tone assessed from photos by two raters introduces potential measurement error, and dichotomization at 0.5 is somewhat arbitrary", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone measurement error"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [119]}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses using alternative dichotomization thresholds yielded similar results", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["alternative thresholds"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [118]}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[142, 142]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "generalizability subheading"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "caveat that results may not generalize beyond European men's soccer 2012-2013, no specific analytic action named"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "league-specific effects subheading"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[147, 147]], "assertion": "the null results in Spain/France contradicting the significant effects in Germany/England suggest the hypothesis may be conditionally true, and pooling across leagues may obscure context-specific mechanisms", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league-specific effects"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[148, 148]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "multiple comparisons subheading"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[150, 150]], "assertion": "conducting multiple sensitivity analyses increases Type I error risk, but consistent directions of effect across analyses mitigate this concern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["multiple comparisons"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "clustering and dependence subheading"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 153]], "assertion": "standard errors were clustered by player but referee-level clustering was not accounted for", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [132, 133]}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 153]], "assertion": "a fully crossed random effects model might be more appropriate but would add complexity", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["crossed random effects model"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [131, 133]}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 153]], "assertion": "ignoring referee clustering may slightly underestimate standard errors", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard error estimation"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [131, 132]}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[154, 154]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[155, 155]], "note": "missing data subheading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[156, 156]], "assertion": "approximately 15% of dyads were excluded due to missing skin tone ratings, and if missingness relates to skin tone and outcome, selection bias could occur (direction unclear)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[157, 159]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[160, 161]], "note": "additional findings heading"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "covariate balance subheading"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "light- and dark-skinned players were generally similar on measured characteristics", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["covariate balance"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 166]], "assertion": "height (182.3 vs 181.6 cm, p=0.078), weight (76.4 vs 75.9 kg, p=0.232), and total games (250.6 vs 235.0, p=0.078) were similar between light- and dark-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["height", "weight", "total games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "light-skinned players received significantly more yellow cards on average (33.9 vs 29.8, p=0.010), suggesting possible differences in playing style or referee behavior toward less severe infractions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["yellow cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "position effects subheading"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "some positions (e.g. Center Back, +1.22 pp marginal effect) had higher red card rates, and adjusting for position reduced confounding by playing style", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["player position"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 174]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[175, 176]], "note": "assumptions and checks heading"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "key assumptions subheading"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[178, 178]], "assertion": "the model assumed a linear relationship between predictors and log-odds; diagnostic plots (not shown) suggested reasonable fit", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model specification assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "the model assumed the measured covariates (games, position, league) capture all confounders of the skin tone–red card relationship", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["no unmeasured confounding assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [152]}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "this no-unmeasured-confounding assumption is unlikely to be fully satisfied", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["no unmeasured confounding assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [151]}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "dyads were assumed independent after accounting for player clustering", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [154]}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "referee clustering was not modeled", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [153]}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "with 115,603 observations, the large-sample assumption for logistic regression's asymptotic properties was deemed reasonable", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["large sample assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "violations and mitigations subheading"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "red cards are rare (1.26%), but the sample is judged large enough for logistic regression to remain appropriate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rare outcome"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[185, 185]], "assertion": "clustered data was addressed via clustered standard errors at the player level", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustered standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "the significant league interaction suggests pooled estimates mask important variation", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league interaction"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [161]}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "stratified analyses were conducted", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["stratified analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [160]}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[187, 189]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[190, 191]], "note": "reproducibility heading"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[192, 196]], "assertion": "all analyses were conducted using Python 3.11 with pandas, numpy, statsmodels, and scipy", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software packages"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 198]], "assertion": "the analysis code is provided in final_analysis.py and produces all reported results, with the dataset available at ./data/soccer/soccer.csv", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["final_analysis.py", "soccer.csv"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[199, 203]], "note": "reproduction command code block"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "running the script generates a full analysis report, summary statistics, and visualizations (analysis_results.png)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["analysis_results.png"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[205, 207]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[208, 209]], "note": "final assessment heading"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not supported based on the primary estimand — the adjusted risk difference is small, non-significant, and the CI includes zero", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["primary estimand"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [172]}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "some sensitivity analyses show significance and the effect direction is consistent, but overall the evidence is deemed inconclusive rather than confirmatory", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [171]}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[212, 212]], "assertion": "the preferred skeptical interpretation is that the dataset does not provide strong evidence of differential red card issuance by skin tone, given non-significance, modest effect size, low power, and unmeasured confounding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skeptical interpretation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "an alternative interpretation is offered: consistent direction, significant continuous-specification result, and strong Germany/England effects suggest the hypothesis may hold in some contexts but be masked elsewhere by low power", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["alternative interpretation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "the analysis recommends a future prospective study with a larger sample, behavioral measures, referee-level implicit-bias data, and league-stratified analysis, implying these were not available here", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research design"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[217, 219]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[220, 221]], "note": "deliverables heading"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 222]], "assertion": "deliverable: primary estimand = adjusted risk difference 0.172 pp (95% CI [-0.017, 0.361]; p=0.074)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["primary estimand"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[223, 223]], "assertion": "deliverable: secondary estimand = adjusted odds ratio 1.153 (95% CI [0.986, 1.347]; p=0.074)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["secondary estimand"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "deliverable: logistic regression on 115,603 dyads adjusting for games, position, league, with clustered SE by player (1,419 clusters)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model details"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[225, 225]], "assertion": "deliverable conclusion: NOT SUPPORTED — hypothesized direction but not significant, inconclusive due to low power and CI including zero", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "deliverable: reproducible code final_analysis.py generates all results", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["final_analysis.py"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[227, 229]], "note": "blank/section-separator scaffolding"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[230, 231]], "note": "author and date lines"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[232, 232]], "assertion": "a two-sided significance level of α = 0.05 was used throughout the analysis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["significance level"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[233, 234]], "note": "blank line and tool-output closing marker"}]}}